{
  "_meta": {
    "label": "Custom-prepared from manual research",
    "preparedBy": "coding agent (Claude), from general knowledge of how Kenyan public sites are usually laid out",
    "date": "2026-11-03",
    "caveat": "No site was contacted. Every rule is a hypothesis about common paths (WordPress and Drupal conventions plus typical government labels) held at confidence 0.3 to 0.6, to be confirmed or replaced by a gated bounded probe and by review. Rules discovered from crawled links only propose additions for review. Paths are matched against the URL path only; hosts and scope stay in the manifest policy.",
    "publisherNote": "2026-11-03 (Lane E): publisher families ke/publisher/* for the priority publishers (parliament, nlc, cob, oag, gazette). Parliament, NLC and COB rules were derived from links on their home pages fetched through the gate; OAG rules come from its home page links at www.oagkenya.go.ke (the apex host fails TLS: wildcard certificate); Gazette rules are hypotheses (kenyagazette.go.ke does not resolve in DNS). NLC and COB publish files through WordPress Download Manager: listing pages link /download/<slug>/ package pages whose file link is ?wpdmdl=<id> (the crawler treats that as a file link). Lands (lands.go.ke) rules come from its home page links: /gazette-notices, /public-notices, /downloads, /active-tenders. NLC package pages carry the file link in a data-downloadurl attribute."
  },
